    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d623-a3">

                <pb facs="0745" n="685" sameAs="frus:frus1895p1/pg685"/>

                <opener><seg rendition="#center">[Inclosure 3 in No. 429.]</seg></opener>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">Lord Kimberley to Mr.
                            Bayard</hi>.</head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Foreign Office</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1895-05-04"><hi rendition="#italic">May 4,
                        1895</hi></date>.</dateline></opener>
                <p><hi rendition="#small-caps">Your Excellency</hi>: With reference to my note of
                    the 21st of March last on the subject of the proposed regulations for preventing
                    collisions <pb facs="0746" n="686" xml:id="pg686"/> at sea, I have the honor to
                    state that the provisions as to sound signals are about to be considered by a
                    select committee of the House of Commons, and that it is impossible at present
                    to fix the date of the issue of the order in council.</p>
                <p>I have, etc.,</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Kimberley</hi>.</signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
